From be88c8d2a300938426a796a797ee8da755642e7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "zheng.ziyang" <zheng.ziyang@zte.com.cn>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 15:03:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] add rvv optimized mem function
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In glibc, I introduced RVV (RISC-V Vector Extension) optimized implementations for core memory and string functions, including memichr, memcmp, memcpy, memmove, memrchr, memset, rawmemchr, and strlen. These vectorized routines leverage RISC-V’s parallel processing capabilities to significantly improve performance in bulk data operations.

Additionally, I integrated the ifunc mechanism for RISC-V, enabling runtime dispatch to the most efficient implementation based on the underlying hardware features. This ensures both portability across diverse RISC-V platforms and optimal performance where vector extensions are available.

Key improvements:

Performance gains: Vectorized routines accelerate common memory operations.
Runtime adaptability: ifunc dispatch selects the best implementation dynamically.
Ecosystem advancement: Strengthens glibc’s support for RISC-V, enhancing its role in high-performance and general-purpose computing.

Signed-off-by: Shangcheng Huang <huang.shangcheng@zte.com.cn>
